## 2026-11-01T14:25Z - Claude Fable 5.1 (as this session reports itself)
- Discussion, decided (Julian): pi/ stays CyborgOS's - "CyborgOS for the Pi" is a deliverable in its own right: cosd with its services and the vCPC running on the Pi, one install, usable by a CPC game (through Streamer or NTC's classes) without CyborgOS on the CPC at all. The move of pi/ to NTC is dropped (nothing was moved). Agreed shape: services are location-independent; the Pi is the coprocessor (Streamer direction) or the processor (the vCPC on the Pi, the CPC its keys, discs and screen); a program runs on the Pi by default when it's there, local when it touches the CPC's hardware or is Locomotive BASIC; a new NTC target cplink (;@base cyborgos) binds Float / Store / VDP / Audio to the Pi locally and Keys / FileSystem to the CPC over the link in reverse; CyborgOS on the CPC shows the Pi's slots as its own. Needs: the vCPC's console as a socket, a slot service in cosd as paths (VCPC:n/RUN, IN, OUT, PS), the CPC's drives served to the Pi (the reverse of disk.js).
- files: ANALYSIS.LOG

