## 2026-11-04T10:11Z - Claude Opus 4.8 (what the harness reports for this turn) - GRU / MIND (the model as a port), Cynthia, and k-trit weights
- GRU and MIND: the generative net served the way the decision services are (MODEL on a port, RATS
  a front). MIND [v:]file loads a GEN.MDL and opens a port named after it (GEN.MDL -> port GEN); the
  net and its hidden state live in MIND's slot. GRU model is the terminal - you type, it carries on,
  the state kept on the server across turns. Port protocol in ASCII codes: ? (shape), R (reset),
  S n (seed), F c (feed, no noise), G c amp (feed with noise) - each gives the next code.
  apps/gru/{MIND,GRU}.bas + CybSys.cls; help GRU.HLP / MIND.HLP; on disc 8 and MSX. "The model is
  a port": a MIND can be kept, moved (RMOVE) or shared while clients come and go.
- Cynthia: a second model, CYNTHIA.MDL - a chitchat "ELIZA killer", trained on short exchanges
  (tools/gen/cynthia_corpus.py). Served and talked to the same way (MIND CYNTHIA, GRU CYNTHIA). On
  the vCPC it converses but garbles words (its dialogue corpus is harder than GEN's structured
  BASIC for a slot-sized net) - a slow, limited toy by design.
- k-trit weights (Julian's idea: 2 trits is better than 1 and faster than a byte; 4 and 8 too, via
  bit planes). Net now reads K balanced-trit weights as K ternary planes, Horner-combined in DotK
  (acc = acc*3 + Trit.Dot(plane) - add/sub only, no multiply, at any K). qgru.py quantises to
  {-L..L}, exports K planes row-interleaved (GEN.MDL v2, a K byte in the header); train.py --trits,
  sample.py and mktest.py follow. test/net_t regenerated at K=2 and the Z80 matches the PC reference
  byte for byte. K=4 (81 levels, a byte) / K=8 (two bytes) are a --trits flag away, no Z80 change;
  the table-lookup inner loop is the documented next speed step (cyborgos-generative.md).
- The shipped GEN.MDL was undertrained (greedy collapsed to spaces - blank output). Fixed three
  ways: a focused corpus (gen_focus.py), a sharper loss (train.py --losstemp 6, gradient-only), and
  2 trits a weight. Shipped GEN / CYNTHIA: H=64, 2-trit, ~29.5K (fit the 32K a slot loads). On the
  vCPC, "For i = 1 To 10" -> "Print i / Next / End Sub", clean NTC BASIC - at 1 trit it wrote "Froo".
- The architecture conversation is recorded as design, not built: ports as a Mixture of Experts
